WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.840
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:06.140
If you’re traveling deep in the American
Midwest, through the barren plains of Nebraska

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:11.559
you’ll pass a tiny collection of buildings,
all but one of them are abandoned and decaying,

00:00:11.559 --> 00:00:14.640
you’ll probably pass by and think nothing
more about it.

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:23.590
But this is the smallest town in all of America,
with a population of just one, Elsie Eiler.

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:30.039
Monowi is the only officially incorporated
municipality in the United States with a population

00:00:30.039 --> 00:00:31.340
of just one.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:35.400
Sure you may know a weird friend who moved
out of his mother’s basement into a mobile

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.150
home in the forest, because he thinks the
government have tapped his phone and put a

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:44.440
camera in his box of Cheerios, but that doesn’t
count, unlike Monowi, your crazy friend’s

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.050
trailer is not officially a town.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:53.390
But Monowi wasn’t always so tiny, it was
once a thriving town, a small town, but a

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:54.570
town nonetheless.

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:59.100
Monowi was founded in 1902 by European settlers
from the Czech Republic.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:03.920
It reached its peak in the 1930s, when it
boasted a handsome population of 150, there

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:04.920
was even a high school in Monowi.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:10.570
But the draw of the big city and the jobs
it offers was too great and one by one the

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:14.720
city’s younger residents moved away from
Monowi, including Elsie’s own children.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:20.820
By the late 1900s all that was left was Elsie
and her husband Rudy.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:24.680
Despite there only being the two of them they
had a nice little place to call home, Rudy

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:28.230
ran the local library and Elsie ran the tavern.

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:32.920
You might be wondering why a town with a grand
population of two, needs a library and a tavern.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:37.560
But the two establishments get quite a lot
of custom from passing travelers and visiting

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:42.670
farmers from nearby towns, who are probably
quite thankful to stumble across Elsie’s

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:46.350
one-woman beer shack, because this is the
middle of absolutely nowhere.

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:53.409
Unfortunately, in 2004 half of the town of
Monowi tragically died.

00:01:53.409 --> 00:01:58.831
Rudy sadly passed away and so the town sign
had to be changed from a population of 2 to

00:01:58.831 --> 00:02:00.049
just 1.

00:02:00.049 --> 00:02:06.130
But good old Elsie, as devastated as she was,
continued running the tavern and library all

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:09.200
by herself and still does to this day.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.630
She spends most of her days socialising with
the vast assortment of visitors that pass

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:16.700
through the town and stop for one of her famous
homemade burgers.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:19.780
But it doesn’t stop there.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:25.670
Since Elsie is Monowi’s only resident she
is also the self-elected town Mayor as well

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:27.620
as bartender and librarian.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:33.180
Running a town is no small feat, certain legal
obligations have to be met, even if it is

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:34.860
only for one person.

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:41.720
Elsie has to pay herself taxes and she has
to grant her own liquor license to run the

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:42.720
tavern.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:46.760
She also has to produce a municipal road plan
every year to secure state funding to keep

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:48.910
its four street lights running.

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:53.630
Monowi must be the only town in America where
you can get served a burger and a beer by

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:54.670
the town Mayor.

00:02:54.670 --> 00:03:00.940
Or maybe not, because thirty-minutes down
the road from Monowi is a little town called

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:04.819
Gross, yeah, seriously, someone named a town
Gross.

00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:08.560
Gross is twice the size of Monowi, with a
grand population of two.

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:14.240
Man and wife Mary and Mike Finnegan are the
town’s only residents, and just like Elsie

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:19.300
of Monowi, they run a tavern and Mike is also
self-elected town mayor.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:25.000
Gross and Monowi are representative of a larger
problem going on across the Great Plains of

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.000
America.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:29.740
People are rapidly abandoning small towns
in search of better jobs and opportunities

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:31.430
in large cities.

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:35.230
Large chain stores are also eradicating the
need for farms.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:40.120
But Elsie is staying strong and stubbornly
refuses to move, despite the fact that she

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:44.849
actually lives in a ghost town, a few years
ago this was one of the town’s main streets,

00:03:44.849 --> 00:03:46.890
now overgrown with vegetation.

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:51.770
The local church is boarded up and all the
houses, except Elsie’s, are decaying into

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:52.860
the ground.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:57.220
She likes to have a laugh with herself though,
the Monowi Inn advertises “the coldest beer

00:03:57.220 --> 00:04:13.700
in town” yeah, it’s also the only beer

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:15.910
in town.

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:21.979
Thanks for watching.

